finding: The stock high-refresh ACK rate and queue-overflow disconnect are fixed, but valid new operations still bypass pacing: intent.ts:333,365–375 sets _unsent on every record and sends the oldest pending batch on each subsequent flush, even at the very same tick. Two record/flush pairs per 360 Hz frame can sustain 720 packets/s before ACKs; the rooms requestBot path already flushes synchronously (examples/rooms/src/network.ts:236–238). upstream.test.ts only introduces one operation and misses this. Queue eviction can also lose an operation permanently when its caller keeps flushing without recording or supplying a new clock (intent.ts:338–340,365–375); press.node.ts now explicitly advances that clock and exercises only the opted-in retry. The cap throws synchronously in record instead of disconnecting, but an uncaught throw still escapes a game's input sampling callback (intent.ts:320–321, examples/rooms/src/network.ts:207–210); there is no recoverable refusal path supplied by IntentSender.
